adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set at runtime, `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`. If the request also omits the header, `req.headers["calcom-webhook-secret"]` is also `undefined`, so the condition becomes `undefined !== undefined` which is `false`, and the request is accepted. That is a fail-open authentication bypass introduced by the diff, allowing unauthenticated calls to proceed to credential create/update logic (subject only to other env-gated conditions like `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED`).
